e spec. A comment above it gives the reason for each directive.\n- **`get_response`** now calls a new `_answer` method with the old body unchanged, sets `Content-Security-Policy` on the result, and returns it. Its docstring is kept.\n\nChecks:\n- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_dashboard.py`: 20 passed.\n- `uv run ruff check .`: all checks passed.\n\nI did not run the full pytest suite or the web checks, since the spec lists only these two commands. `api/guard.py` and the web build are untouched, so `LoopbackGuard`'s frame-ancestors header is still there alongside the new one.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: a 404 under `api` or `assets` is raised as an `HTTPException` rather than returned, so that error response does not get the new header. The spec's wording covers only responses `DashboardFiles` returns, so I left it that way.", "ttft_ms": 2333, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 24663, "uuid": "9e1f33f1-4381-4da1-9c5b-c7283da215fd", "ttft_stream_ms": 2251, "time_to_request_ms": 458, "first_content_frame_ms": 2251, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
